Law is fairly settled that, for attracting the charges under Section 498A of IPC, prosecution is duty bound to prove following essential ingredients :-
"(1) A woman was married;
(2) She was subjected to cruelty;
(3) Such cruelty consisted in - (i) any lawful conduct as was likely to drive such woman to commit suicide or to cause grave injury or danger to her life, limb or health whether mental or physical;
(ii) harm to such woman with a view to coercing her to meet unlawful demand for property or valuable security or on account of failure of such woman or any of her relations to meet the lawful demand ;
(iii) the woman was subjected to such cruelty by her husband or any relation of her husband."
11. Section 306 of the IPC deals with abetment to commit suicide.

Ingredients of this section are as under :
 (1) There was suicide of a person;
 (2) It was committed in consequence of abetment of the  accused.
